  "name": "FurCamp Michigan",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "FurCamp Michigan, formerly Northern Michigan FurCamp, is an 18+ furry camping convention in Michigan, organized by FCM Events LLC. It began in 2022 in the Traverse City area and was a \"traveling furry camp\" at several sites before settling at the Lake Michigan Recreation Area in Free Soil, with two large group campsites; tents only are allowed, and activities include community-run events, swimming, games and s'mores. It was renamed FurCamp Michigan in September 2024, when it moved toward the middle of the state, and became a yearly event instead of twice a year. Its charity is the Skegemog Raptor Sanctuary.",
